From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: light.msstyles: Stained Glass scroll bars

Light's scroll bars were bordered boxes: a grey-outlined arrow button and
thumb on a white track, with a gripper on the thumb. This draws them flat,
in the Windows 10 manner, as our own artwork: a #f0f0f0 track; a borderless
thumb, inset 2 px from the long edges, #cdcdcd, #a6a6a6 when hot, #606060
pressed; arrow buttons that take the track's colour (hot #dadada, pressed
#606060) with a small solid triangle glyph (#606060; black hot, white
pressed, #bfbfbf disabled); no gripper (its parts are removed from the
theme, so none is drawn). The Scrollbar system colour is the track's.

The SVGs are generated by theme/scrollbar.py in the wine-sg repository
(the image grids are the ones Light's INI declares); build.sh renders them
to the .bmp files the theme packs, as for patch 0031.

Gate: test/theme-gate.sh draws the scroll bar's parts from the installed
theme and checks their colours pixel by pixel, and that Light's border grey
is gone.
---
